<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-surf-drip" category="Clean" order="130" instrument="guitar" style="Surf">
  <description>Wet, dripping surf: a tube spring tank placed before the amp, as with the classic outboard reverb unit, into a loud bright blackface driving 15-inch speakers. Staccato tremolo picking on the low strings makes the springs splash and drip. Dwell sets how hard the tank is hit.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Surf</tag><tag>Spring Reverb</tag><tag>Wet</tag><tag>Twang</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fender_Reverb_Unit" title="Fender Reverb Unit (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://www.premierguitar.com/pro-advice/on-the-bench/fender-6g15-reverb-unit" title="Premier Guitar: On the Bench, 1964 6G15 reverb unit"/>
    <source url="https://wiki.surfguitar101.com/ReverbFaq" title="Surf Guitar 101 wiki: 6G15 reverb FAQ"/>
    <source url="https://www.tdpri.com/threads/how-do-you-set-your-6g15-reverb-unit.981137/" title="TDPRI: how do you set your 6G15 reverb unit"/>
    <source url="https://www.fuzzfaced.net/dick-dale-stratocaster-beast.html" title="Fuzzfaced: Dick Dale and the Stratocaster"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
